	<key>readme</key>
	<string>See what your Mac's hosts file overrides, and why, and change it in seconds.

Type `hosts` to list your entries. Each one shows its IP, its comment, when it was added and the section it sits in (for example "Docker Desktop"). System entries are listed last. Keep typing to search hostnames, IPs, comments and sections.

* **Enter** turns an entry off (comments it out) or back on
* **⌥ Enter** removes it (a backup is kept at /etc/hosts.bak)
* **⌘C** copies the line

**Add an entry** by typing a hostname that isn't in the file:

* `hosts mysite.test My local site` adds `mysite.test` for 127.0.0.1 with the comment "My local site"
* `hosts example.com 10.0.0.5 New server test` points `example.com` at 10.0.0.5 (the IP can also come first)
* A pasted URL is reduced to its hostname

Changes ask for your administrator password and flush the DNS cache. System entries such as `localhost` can't be changed.

The keyword can be changed in Configure Workflow.</string>
